From 213f00cb080691d96d3f7cae648914b071ec3e71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Des Flynn <des@desflynn.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:22:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Always show when a halted turn stopped in the assistant
 footer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The footer hid the end time behind hover/tap whenever the turn duration was
known, so most turns showed only "Worked for X". It now reads
"Worked for 1m 3s · Stopped at 16:04", with the weekday within the week and
the full date after that. The semantic-markdown plugin drops its build stamp
line under every message; render failures still show the build.
